sequenceDiagram
    actor Main
    participant Billing as BillingService
    participant Usage as UsageRepository
    participant Catalog as ProductCatalog
    participant Trial as TrialPolicy

    Main->>Billing: generateMonthlyBill user 1, Feb 2025
    Billing->>Usage: getUsage user 1, Feb 2025
    Usage-->>Billing: JIRA used 20 days
    Billing->>Catalog: getProduct JIRA
    Catalog-->>Billing: JIRA, 10 dollars per month
    Billing->>Trial: billableDays JIRA, 20
    Trial-->>Billing: 20 billable days
    Note over Billing: amount equals 10 times 20 divided by 28, Feb 2025 has 28 days
    Billing-->>Main: line item JIRA 7.14 dollars

    Main->>Billing: generateMonthlyBill user 1, Feb 2024
    Billing->>Usage: getUsage user 1, Feb 2024
    Usage-->>Billing: JIRA used 20 days
    Billing->>Catalog: getProduct JIRA
    Catalog-->>Billing: JIRA, 10 dollars per month
    Billing->>Trial: billableDays JIRA, 20
    Trial-->>Billing: 20 billable days
    Note over Billing: amount equals 10 times 20 divided by 29, Feb 2024 is a leap year with 29 days
    Billing-->>Main: line item JIRA 6.90 dollars

    Note over Main,Trial: same raw usage, different real months, different correct totals - this is the fix for the practice code's hardcoded 30 day divisor
